Title: Wire class_trace and n_bib_entries into RunSummary
Created: 2026-05-29
Author: Claude
Blocked-by: 0384

--- log ---
2026-05-29T00:00Z Claude created — finding #3 from the mart audit (0383); real data loss

--- body ---
## Context

Finding #3 from 0383. `RunSummary` (exp2_mart.py:99-114) declares
`class_trace: list[str] | None` and `n_bib_entries: int | None`, and both
keys are present and non-null in **80/80** source run JSONs (populated by
`extract_arm_single_turn.py:194,197` and `extract_arm_multi_turn.py`).

But `_build_run_records` in `build_exp2_mart.py:242-251` constructs
`RunSummary(...)` without passing either field, so both are null in every
mart record. The field exists, the data exists, the wire is missing — silent
data loss.

## Approach

In `build_exp2_mart.py:_build_run_records`, add to the `RunSummary(...)` call:

```python
class_trace=meta.get("class_trace"),
n_bib_entries=meta.get("n_bib_entries"),
```

Note `class_trace` arrives from extraction already as a `list[str]` (e.g.
`["report"]`), matching the schema type — no split needed here. Then
regenerate `experiments/derived/exp2_mart.jsonl` via the Makefile target and
commit the updated artifact.

## First test

Extend `tests/test_build_exp2_mart.py`: a run whose source JSON carries
`class_trace` and `n_bib_entries` produces a `RunSummary` with both
populated (not None).

## Definition of done

- [ ] `_build_run_records` wires `class_trace` and `n_bib_entries`
- [ ] `experiments/derived/exp2_mart.jsonl` regenerated; class_trace and
      n_bib_entries non-null where the source has them
- [ ] 0384's adherence guard passes for these two keys
- [ ] Unit test added; Makefile DAG prerequisites/targets still match the
      script's actual reads/writes
- [ ] `make check` green
